From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 1047 redfin: AppleCLCD says why it did not start

The one silent path out of AppleCLCD::start() is the provider's start,
and a boot with no "SWEET FB:" line at all cannot tell which of the two it
was: the display node never matched, or it matched and its provider failed.
Both look identical in the klog — no line. Log the provider failure and
whether the display node was reached at all, so a dead present path names
itself instead of needing a guess.

Boot klog gains, on the failing boots only:
  "SWEET FB: AppleCLCD::start: provider start failed (...)"  provider did not start
  "SWEET FB: no boot framebuffer ..."                        already there; PE console empty
The healthy path is unchanged: it still logs "SWEET FB: AppleCLCD WxH stride ...".
---
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -191,6 +191,13 @@ AppleCLCD::start(IOService *provider)
 {
 	PE_Video video;
 
+	/*
+	 * Reaching here means the 'sweet,display' node matched. Without this line a klog with
+	 * no "SWEET FB:" at all is ambiguous: node never matched, or matched and the provider
+	 * (SweetPlatformExpert's nub) failed to start. The second case used to be silent.
+	 */
+	IOLog("SWEET FB: AppleCLCD::start: display node matched (provider %s)\n",
+	    provider != NULL ? "present" : "NULL");
 	if (!IOService::start(provider)) {
+		IOLog("SWEET FB: AppleCLCD::start: provider start failed\n");
 		return false;
 	}
 	PE_current_console(&video);
